From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TinyYana <yanasakuranight@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 14:50:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Lophinya: GriefPrevention-specific scheduler redispatch

Companion to the folia-supported allow-list: without this, GriefPrevention's
onEnable() still throws on its first sync scheduler call (DeliverClaimBlocksTask,
a fan-out task with no single player/location context), aborting registration of
all 68 @EventHandlers - the actual claim-protection logic - before any of them
run.

LophinyaGriefPreventionCompat redispatches exactly three named, version-locked
task classes to GlobalRegionScheduler - the three whose scheduling call sits
directly in onEnable() and would otherwise block it:
  - DeliverClaimBlocksTask (only the player==null fan-out variant; verified via
    real GriefPrevention 16.18.7 source that this variant has no single-region
    context requirement)
  - EntityCleanupTask (schedule-only fix; its cleanup logic still touches
    world-wide entity state and is expected to fail/no-op on its first
    non-global-owned touch - a known, accepted degradation, not attempted here)
  - FindUnusedClaimsTask (its run() already only fans out via
    runTaskAsynchronously, already restored by patch 0024)

Not a general sync-to-GlobalRegionScheduler shim (DEC-05's rejected S-3) - a
hard-coded allow-list of three specific classes from one version-locked jar.
Dispatched tasks are tracked and cancelled on plugin disable (same bug class
patch 0024's hardening round fixed for the async scheduler).

Kill switch: -Dlophinya.compat.griefprevention=true (default OFF - the most
reflection-dependent hook so far; the original design proposal asked for
opt-in, not opt-out).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/compat/LophinyaGriefPreventionCompat.java b/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/compat/LophinyaGriefPreventionCompat.java
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..491edece82899c448635df295f8ecb251a907786
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/main/java/fun/bm/lophinya/compat/LophinyaGriefPreventionCompat.java
@@ -0,0 +1,233 @@
+package fun.bm.lophinya.compat;
+
+import com.mojang.logging.LogUtils;
+import io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.scheduler.ScheduledTask;
+import org.bukkit.Bukkit;
+import org.bukkit.craftbukkit.scheduler.CraftTask;
+import org.bukkit.entity.Player;
+import org.bukkit.plugin.Plugin;
+import org.slf4j.Logger;
+
+import java.lang.reflect.Field;
+import java.nio.file.Files;
+import java.nio.file.Path;
+import java.security.MessageDigest;
+import java.util.HexFormat;
+import java.util.List;
+import java.util.Map;
+import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;
+import java.util.concurrent.CopyOnWriteArrayList;
+
+/**
+ * Lophinya: GriefPrevention-specific scheduler redispatch.
+ *
+ * <p>Companion to {@link LophinyaFoliaSupportedAllowlist}: that patch only lets GriefPrevention
+ * 16.18.7 past the load gate. Without this class, its {@code onEnable()} still throws on the very
+ * first sync scheduler registration ({@code DeliverClaimBlocksTask}, a fan-out task with no single
+ * player/location - see project-docs
+ * {@code evidence/20260728-griefprevention-core-shim-implementation-plan.md} §0), which aborts the
+ * rest of {@code onEnable()} before any of its 68 {@code @EventHandler}s (the actual claim
+ * protection logic) get registered.
+ *
+ * <p>This redispatches four named, version-locked task classes, each individually verified
+ * against the real official GriefPrevention 16.18.7 source (not decompiled):
+ * <ul>
+ *   <li>{@code DeliverClaimBlocksTask} - has two variants distinguished only by its private
+ *       {@code player} field's value: {@code null} is a fan-out task with no single
+ *       player/location context (dispatched to {@link io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.scheduler.GlobalRegionScheduler});
+ *       non-null is a single known player, scheduled one tick apart from inside the fan-out
+ *       task's own {@code run()} (dispatched to that player's
+ *       {@link io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.scheduler.EntityScheduler}). Neither is a guess at
+ *       region ownership; see B1/B2 boundary discussion in {@code DECISIONS.md} DEC-19</li>
+ *   <li>{@code EntityCleanupTask} (schedule-only fix, global region - its own cleanup logic still
+ *       touches world-wide entity state and is expected to fail/no-op on its first
+ *       non-global-owned touch; this is a known, accepted degradation, not something this class
+ *       tries to fix)</li>
+ *   <li>{@code FindUnusedClaimsTask} (global region - its {@code run()} already only fans out via
+ *       {@code runTaskAsynchronously}, which patch 0024 already restored)</li>
+ *   <li>{@code PvPImmunityValidationTask} (single known player for its whole lifetime, dispatched
+ *       to that player's {@code EntityScheduler})</li>
+ * </ul>
+ *
+ * <p><b>Not yet handled</b> (see project-docs
+ * {@code evidence/20260728-griefprevention-core-shim-implementation-plan.md} §2.4/§2.5):
+ * {@code SiegeCheckupTask} needs a genuine two-hop redesign (it reads both an attacker's and a
+ * defender's location in one {@code run()}, which can span two regions - simply relocating the
+ * whole call is not safe), and the
+ * {@code CleanupUnusedClaimPreTask}→{@code CleanupUnusedClaimTask} handoff needs chunk-scoped
+ * dispatch via {@code claim.getChunks()} that the proposal itself flags as an open design
+ * question. Both fall through to stock rejection for now - logged, not fatal.
+ *
+ * <p>This is <b>not</b> a general "route sync tasks to GlobalRegionScheduler" shim (that is
+ * exactly {@code DEC-05}'s S-3, explicitly rejected) - it is a hard-coded allow-list of specific
+ * classes from one version-locked jar, each individually confirmed to have no single-region
+ * context requirement (or, for the per-player variants, dispatched to that exact player's own
+ * scheduler rather than the global one).
+ *
+ * <p>Tasks dispatched here are tracked so they can be cancelled when the plugin is disabled -
+ * {@link #cancelAll(Plugin)} is called from the same disable hook patch 0024 added for the
+ * restored async scheduler, closing the same class of "disabled plugin's task keeps running
+ * forever" bug that hardening round fixed for async tasks (DEC-17).
+ *
+ * <p>Kill switch: {@code -Dlophinya.compat.griefprevention=true} - unlike patch 0024/0025, this
+ * defaults to <b>off</b>. It is the most novel, most reflection-dependent hook in this project so
+ * far, and the original design proposal deliberately asked for opt-in rather than opt-out.
+ */
+public final class LophinyaGriefPreventionCompat {
+
+    private static final Logger LOGGER = LogUtils.getLogger();
+
+    public static final boolean ENABLED =
+        "true".equalsIgnoreCase(System.getProperty("lophinya.compat.griefprevention", "false"));
+
+    /** GriefPrevention 16.18.7, s01-installed version. See evidence/20260728-t09*.md. */
+    private static final String EXPECTED_SHA256 =
+        "45E9907C61222E559ED2E099FFEE0EDE706A21243A31D7DB549BAF678708FDF0";
+
+    private static final String DELIVER_CLAIM_BLOCKS_TASK = "me.ryanhamshire.GriefPrevention.DeliverClaimBlocksTask";
+    private static final String ENTITY_CLEANUP_TASK = "me.ryanhamshire.GriefPrevention.EntityCleanupTask";
+    private static final String FIND_UNUSED_CLAIMS_TASK = "me.ryanhamshire.GriefPrevention.FindUnusedClaimsTask";
+    private static final String PVP_IMMUNITY_VALIDATION_TASK = "me.ryanhamshire.GriefPrevention.PvPImmunityValidationTask";
+
+    private static final Map<Path, String> SHA_CACHE = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
+    private static final Map<Plugin, List<ScheduledTask>> DISPATCHED = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
+
+    private LophinyaGriefPreventionCompat() {
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * @param task   the task about to be rejected by stock Folia's {@code CraftScheduler.handle}
+     * @param delay  the delay in ticks, as passed to {@code handle}
+     * @param period the task's period ({@code CraftTask.getPeriod()} is package-private to
+     *               {@code org.bukkit.craftbukkit.scheduler}, so the caller passes it through)
+     * @return the same task (already scheduled on the global region), or {@code null} if this task
+     *         does not match one of the three known-safe classes and should fall through to the
+     *         normal rejection path
+     */
+    public static CraftTask tryDispatch(final CraftTask task, final long delay, final long period) {
+        if (!ENABLED) {
+            return null;
+        }
+        try {
+            final Plugin plugin = task.getOwner();
+            if (plugin == null || task.rTask == null || !isThisJar(plugin)) {
+                return null;
+            }
+
+            final String className = task.rTask.getClass().getName();
+            final ScheduledTask scheduled;
+            if (ENTITY_CLEANUP_TASK.equals(className)) {
+                scheduled = Bukkit.getGlobalRegionScheduler()
+                    .runDelayed(plugin, ignored -> task.run(), Math.max(delay, 1L));
+            } else if (FIND_UNUSED_CLAIMS_TASK.equals(className)) {
+                scheduled = Bukkit.getGlobalRegionScheduler()
+                    .runAtFixedRate(plugin, ignored -> task.run(), Math.max(delay, 1L), Math.max(period, 1L));
+            } else if (DELIVER_CLAIM_BLOCKS_TASK.equals(className)) {
+                // Two variants of the same class, distinguished only by the private `player`
+                // field's value at construction time - both verified against real GriefPrevention
+                // 16.18.7 source. player == null: fan-out task, no single-player/location context,
+                // safe on the global region. player != null: single known player, scheduled one
+                // tick apart from inside the fan-out task's own run() - safe on that player's
+                // EntityScheduler. Reflection failure means "unknown", not "assume global" - fail
+                // closed to stock rejection rather than guess.
+                final PlayerFieldResult pf = readPlayerField(task.rTask);
+                if (!pf.readable()) {
+                    return null;
+                }
+                if (pf.player() == null) {
+                    scheduled = Bukkit.getGlobalRegionScheduler()
+                        .runAtFixedRate(plugin, ignored -> task.run(), Math.max(delay, 1L), Math.max(period, 1L));
+                } else {
+                    final ScheduledTask s = pf.player().getScheduler()
+                        .runDelayed(plugin, ignored -> task.run(), null, Math.max(delay, 1L));
+                    if (s == null) {
+                        // Entity already invalid/removed by schedule time - not an error, the
+                        // per-player task simply has nothing to do.
+                        return task;
+                    }
+                    scheduled = s;
+                }
+            } else if (PVP_IMMUNITY_VALIDATION_TASK.equals(className)) {
+                // Single known player for the task's whole lifetime (constructor-only field,
+                // never null) - self-reschedules via the same call site, so this branch also
+                // handles its own repeat checks.
+                final PlayerFieldResult pf = readPlayerField(task.rTask);
+                if (!pf.readable() || pf.player() == null) {
+                    return null;
+                }
+                final ScheduledTask s = pf.player().getScheduler()
+                    .runDelayed(plugin, ignored -> task.run(), null, Math.max(delay, 1L));
+                if (s == null) {
+                    return task;
+                }
+                scheduled = s;
+            } else {
+                return null;
+            }
+
+            DISPATCHED.computeIfAbsent(plugin, p -> new CopyOnWriteArrayList<>()).add(scheduled);
+            LOGGER.warn("[Lophinya] GriefPrevention: redispatched {} to GlobalRegionScheduler "
+                + "(delay={}, period={}) - this is a named, version-locked allow-list entry, not a "
+                + "general sync-to-global shim", className, delay, period);
+            return task;
+        } catch (final Throwable t) {
+            // ponytail: any failure here must fall through to stock rejection, never silently
+            // "succeed" without actually having scheduled anything.
+            LOGGER.warn("[Lophinya] GriefPrevention redispatch failed (falling through to stock rejection)", t);
+            return null;
+        }
+    }
+
+    /** Called from the plugin-disable path so a disabled plugin's redispatched tasks stop running. */
+    public static void cancelAll(final Plugin plugin) {
+        final List<ScheduledTask> tasks = DISPATCHED.remove(plugin);
+        if (tasks == null) {
+            return;
+        }
+        for (final ScheduledTask t : tasks) {
+            try {
+                t.cancel();
+            } catch (final Throwable ignored) {
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
+    private static boolean isThisJar(final Plugin plugin) {
+        try {
+            final Path jarPath = Path.of(plugin.getClass().getProtectionDomain().getCodeSource().getLocation().toURI());
+            final String sha256 = SHA_CACHE.computeIfAbsent(jarPath, LophinyaGriefPreventionCompat::hash);
+            return EXPECTED_SHA256.equals(sha256);
+        } catch (final Throwable t) {
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+
+    private static String hash(final Path jarPath) {
+        try {
+            final MessageDigest md = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256");
+            return HexFormat.of().withUpperCase().formatHex(md.digest(Files.readAllBytes(jarPath)));
+        } catch (final Throwable t) {
+            return "<unreadable>";
+        }
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Reads a class's private {@code player} field (the name both {@code DeliverClaimBlocksTask}
+     * and {@code PvPImmunityValidationTask} happen to use). {@code readable=false} means
+     * reflection failed (renamed/removed field upstream) - callers must treat that as "unknown,
+     * do not guess" and fall through to stock rejection, not assume any particular variant.
+     */
+    private static PlayerFieldResult readPlayerField(final Runnable rTask) {
+        try {
+            final Field f = rTask.getClass().getDeclaredField("player");
+            f.setAccessible(true);
+            final Object value = f.get(rTask);
+            return new PlayerFieldResult(true, (value instanceof Player p) ? p : null);
+        } catch (final Throwable t) {
+            return new PlayerFieldResult(false, null);
+        }
+    }
+
+    private record PlayerFieldResult(boolean readable, Player player) {
+    }
+}
diff --git a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
index d01d2e69974f5af5350a684aaac7d1ce25b3782f..ee1ad3b80b9e266d2b0afd7edf0e477339b9d6d2 100644
--- a/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
+++ b/src/main/java/io/papermc/paper/plugin/manager/PaperPluginInstanceManager.java
@@ -274,6 +274,15 @@ class PaperPluginInstanceManager {
         }
         // Lophinya end - restored async scheduler: cancel Bukkit tasks on disable, like Paper does
 
+        // Lophinya start - GriefPrevention-specific scheduler redispatch: cancel any tasks this
+        // plugin had redispatched to GlobalRegionScheduler, same reasoning as the block above -
+        // otherwise a disabled plugin's redispatched tasks would keep running forever.
+        try {
+            fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaGriefPreventionCompat.cancelAll(plugin);
+        } catch (Throwable ignored) {
+        }
+        // Lophinya end - GriefPrevention-specific scheduler redispatch
+
         // Paper start - Folia schedulers
         try {
             this.server.getGlobalRegionScheduler().cancelTasks(plugin);
diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
index 8d094c0afe74b199500f3e8a23ce13d9abf86061..1c37baa7b3cb7bf140f96c93386df9d166ecf8d6 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/scheduler/CraftScheduler.java
@@ -550,6 +550,16 @@ public class CraftScheduler implements BukkitScheduler {
             this.addTask(task);
             return task;
         }
+        // Lophinya start - GriefPrevention-specific scheduler redispatch (opt-in, see
+        // LophinyaGriefPreventionCompat for scope and rationale). Only reached for sync tasks on
+        // the main (non-async) scheduler - exactly the case stock Folia has no home for.
+        if (!this.isAsyncScheduler && task.isSync()) {
+            final CraftTask redispatched = fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaGriefPreventionCompat.tryDispatch(task, delay, task.getPeriod());
+            if (redispatched != null) {
+                return redispatched;
+            }
+        }
+        // Lophinya end - GriefPrevention-specific scheduler redispatch
         throw new UnsupportedOperationException(fun.bm.lophinya.compat.LophinyaSchedulerDiagnostics.reportRejected(
             task.getOwner(), delay, task.getPeriod(), !task.isSync()));
         // Lophinya end - restore Bukkit async scheduler semantics + diagnostic guard
